The maximal ideal at $p$ in $A'$ is generated by $y_3, x_1$ and a third element $g$ whose image in $\kappa [y_2]$ is the prime divisor of $h$ corresponding to $p$. If this prime divisor doesn't divide $h$ twice, then we see that the quadratic form at $p$ looks like <div class="equation">
  \[  y_3^2 - x_1((something)x_1 + (something)y_3 + (unit)g)  \]
</div> and this can never be a square in $\kappa [y_3, x_1, g]$.